  { number := 68, text := "## 3. Terms" },
  { number := 69, text := "" },
  { number := 70, text := "1. `L0` means the laptop coordinator. The crate name is `surmount-coordinator-gui`. `L0` queues prompts. `L0` is not a nested agent." },
  { number := 71, text := "2. The call name `grok-oss gui` is an informative name for that same coordinator. It matches the crate." },
  { number := 72, text := "3. `L1` means the main session." },
  { number := 73, text := "4. `L2` means the coordinator. In this specification the word coordinator means `L2` only." },
  { number := 74, text := "5. `L3` means the specialist. In this specification the word specialist means `L3` only." },
  { number := 75, text := "6. `L4` is not a layer in this specification." },
  { number := 76, text := "7. A nested agent in this specification means `L1`, `L2`, or `L3`." },
  { number := 77, text := "8. A report means a file on disk that passes work from one layer to the next. A report is not a join." },
  { number := 78, text := "9. A write set means the files one work stream changes." },
  { number := 79, text := "10. The task description given to an `L2` means the text that `L2` receives when it is spawned." },
  { number := 80, text := "11. The hierarchical fast path means the three acts in Clause 4.4." },
  { number := 81, text := "12. Approve means the operator approval after which nested exploration and nested implementation start." },
  { number := 82, text := "13. Red then green means a failing test first, then the fix, where Clause 4.13 applies." },
  { number := 83, text := "" },
  { number := 84, text := "## 4. Requirements" },
  { number := 85, text := "" },
  { number := 86, text := "The keywords MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119." },
  { number := 87, text := "" },
  { number := 88, text := "### 4.1 Layers" },
  { number := 89, text := "" },
  { number := 90, text := "1. `L0` SHALL be the laptop coordinator whose crate name is `surmount-coordinator-gui`. `L0` SHALL queue prompts. `L0` SHALL NOT be a nested agent." },
  { number := 91, text := "2. The call name `grok-oss gui` is informative and matches that crate. This specification SHALL NOT state that `L0` merges into a pager dashboard." },
  { number := 92, text := "3. `L1` SHALL be the main session." },
  { number := 93, text := "4. `L2` SHALL be the coordinator. The word coordinator SHALL mean `L2` only." },
  { number := 94, text := "5. `L3` SHALL be the specialist. The word specialist SHALL mean `L3` only." },
  { number := 95, text := "6. There SHALL be no `L4`." },
  { number := 96, text := "7. [0015_Session_Bus.md](0015_Session_Bus.md) does not define `L0`, `L1`, `L2`, or `L3`. This specification SHALL NOT pretend that it does." },
  { number := 97, text := "" },
  { number := 98, text := "### 4.2 Naming" },
  { number := 99, text := "" },
  { number := 100, text := "1. Authors SHALL NOT call a layer a parent, and SHALL NOT call a layer a child, in chat, board titles, spawn descriptions, plans, reports, residual, or docs." },
  { number := 101, text := "2. Authors SHALL NOT compare layers to operating system process trees in those same places." },
  { number := 102, text := "3. This specification SHALL NOT use the phrase child process for an agent. That phrase names a real operating system process in other technical documents. This document does not use it for an agent." },
  { number := 103, text := "4. Files on disk that pass work from one layer to the next SHALL be called reports. They SHALL NOT be called joins." },
  { number := 104, text := "5. When explaining this structure, an author MAY name parallelism that forks work and then joins the results. That permission does not allow calling a layer a parent or a child." },
  { number := 105, text := "" },
  { number := 106, text := "### 4.3 Depth" },
  { number := 107, text := "" },
  { number := 108, text := "When implement work, diagnosis across more than one file, continuous integration, or a regression needs tools, that work SHALL run three layers deep. That includes implement loops." },
  { number := 109, text := "" },
  { number := 110, text := "### 4.4 L1 and the fast path" },
  { number := 111, text := "" },
  { number := 112, text := "1. `L1` duties SHALL be status, spawning an `L2`, waiting, reading short reports, and a board `upsert`." },
  { number := 113, text := "2. `L1` SHALL NOT edit product code, and `L1` SHALL NOT edit docs." },
  { number := 114, text := "3. The hierarchical fast path SHALL be for `L1` only. It SHALL have exactly three acts: one command that answers a host question, one read of a path that was already named, and reading and quoting a report that `L1` asked for." },
  { number := 115, text := "4. This specification SHALL NOT add a fourth act on that path." },
  { number := 116, text := "5. The hierarchical fast path SHALL NOT appear in the task description given to an `L2`." },
  { number := 117, text := "" },
  { number := 118, text := "### 4.5 L2" },
  { number := 119, text := "" },
  { number := 120, text := "1. An `L2` SHALL run at the same time the work that Clause 4.9 allows to run at the same time, spawn an `L3`, wait, read the `L3` report, write one `L2` report, record a board `upsert`, and discard context after that report." },
  { number := 121, text := "2. An `L2` SHALL NOT `grep`, read product files, diagnose, edit, implement, or review." },
  { number := 122, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT use the spawn rule that easy work stays on the `L2`. That rule is nonconforming." },
  { number := 123, text := "4. Authors SHALL NOT use the spawn rule that an `L2` spawns an `L3` only when the slice is hard. That rule is nonconforming." },
  { number := 124, text := "5. An `L2` SHALL NOT compact because it ran implement tools itself. That compaction is nonconforming." },
  { number := 125, text := "6. Operator clarifications SHALL go to the `L2`. The `L3` SHALL stay undisturbed." },
  { number := 126, text := "" },
  { number := 127, text := "### 4.6 L3" },
  { number := 128, text := "" },
  { number := 129, text := "1. An `L3` SHALL be an implementer, a researcher, or a reviewer." },
  { number := 130, text := "2. The `L3` SHALL do the tool work for the jobs in Clause 4.3, aside from the `L1` fast path in Clause 4.4." },
  { number := 131, text := "3. The `L3` SHALL NOT coordinate, and the `L3` SHALL NOT spawn." },
  { number := 132, text := "4. There SHALL be no `L4`. An `L3` SHALL NOT be called a coordinator." },
  { number := 133, text := "" },
  { number := 134, text := "### 4.7 Reports" },
  { number := 135, text := "" },
  { number := 136, text := "1. Reports SHALL be written under `~/.agents/reports/` on the host." },
  { number := 137, text := "2. Reports SHALL NOT be written in the repository." },
  { number := 138, text := "3. A report SHALL state what changed, how it was verified, what remains, and any question for the operator." },
  { number := 139, text := "" },
  { number := 140, text := "### 4.8 Plan gate" },
  { number := 141, text := "" },
  { number := 142, text := "1. While a plan is being written or presented, nested exploration SHALL NOT start, and nested implementation SHALL NOT start." },
  { number := 143, text := "2. Nested exploration and nested implementation SHALL start only after the operator Approve." },
  { number := 144, text := "" },
  { number := 145, text := "### 4.9 Parallelism" },
  { number := 146, text := "" },
  { number := 147, text := "1. Independent work streams with disjoint write sets SHALL run as parallel `L2` coordinators at a sustainable count." },
  { number := 148, text := "2. This specification SHALL NOT be read as setting that count to an integer." },
  { number := 149, text := "3. Work streams that share a file SHALL run in sequence." },
  { number := 150, text := "4. Each `L2` SHALL stay listed until that `L2` writes its own report." },
  { number := 151, text := "5. An `L2` that exits after only spawning SHALL NOT be treated as finished." },
  { number := 152, text := "6. An `L2` that exits without a report SHALL NOT be treated as finished." },
  { number := 153, text := "" },
  { number := 154, text := "### 4.10 Long builds" },
  { number := 155, text := "" },
  { number := 156, text := "1. A long build SHALL get one dedicated `L2`." },
  { number := 157, text := "2. That `L2` SHALL run one job." },
  { number := 158, text := "3. That job SHALL run at nice 19." },
  { number := 159, text := "4. That job SHALL NOT be split into several copies at once." },
  { number := 160, text := "5. That job SHALL NOT be terminated early." },
  { number := 161, text := "6. Other work SHALL continue while that job runs." },
  { number := 162, text := "" },
  { number := 163, text := "### 4.11 Context budget (informative)" },
  { number := 164, text := "" },
  { number := 165, text := "This subsection is informative. It records sampling windows from the product note `FORK.md`, in the part that note calls Economic mode. It does not set a conformance cap. No named product function enforces the figures below." },
  { number := 166, text := "" },
  { number := 167, text := "1. That note records nested `L2` and `L3` sampling capped at 200k, and records that `L1` uses the catalog window of 500k." },
  { number := 168, text := "2. The function that would enforce those figures is unnamed. `FORK.md` records tests in session spawn code. The recorded names are `nested_session_sampling_window_stays_200k_when_catalog_is_500k` and `main_session_sampling_window_is_catalog_500k_even_when_economic_is_on`. Those names are records from that note. They are not an enforcer. This document does not claim those tests were run from here." },
  { number := 169, text := "3. The same note names `refresh_context_used` and records that this function does not copy the catalog window into the nested field. That name is not an enforcer of the 200k figure or the 500k figure." },
  { number := 170, text := "" },
  { number := 171, text := "### 4.12 Finished work" },
  { number := 172, text := "" },
  { number := 173, text := "1. Work is finished only when the approved plan's owed outcome has landed." },
  { number := 174, text := "2. That landing SHALL be checked against files on disk. One passing test is not that landing." },
  { number := 175, text := "3. Remaining work SHALL go to the residual home that project already uses, and the next step there SHALL be the highest value next step." },
  { number := 176, text := "4. This specification SHALL NOT be read as an instruction to recreate `INVENTORY.md` or `RESIDUAL.md` in this specifications repository." },
  { number := 177, text := "5. This specification has its own leftover list in Clause 6." },
  { number := 178, text := "" },
  { number := 179, text := "### 4.13 Tests" },
  { number := 180, text := "" },
  { number := 181, text := "1. Where a change is a behavior change, authors SHALL observe a failing test first and SHALL make the fix after that failure. That order is red then green." },
  { number := 182, text := "2. Where a change is not a behavior change, this specification does not ask for a failing test first." },
  { number := 183, text := "" },
  { number := 184, text := "### 4.14 Process repair" },
  { number := 185, text := "" },
  { number := 186, text := "1. When the operator repeats an instruction, that repetition SHALL be treated as a process defect." },
  { number := 187, text := "2. The repair SHALL land in a durable place. A durable place is an `AGENTS.md` file, a skill, or a check." },
  { number := 188, text := "3. A chat promise SHALL NOT be that repair." },
  { number := 189, text := "4. [0006_RSI.md](0006_RSI.md) states that a chat reminder is not a durable tool. That statement is not this repetition rule. The repetition rule is this clause." },
  { number := 190, text := "" },
  { number := 191, text := "## 5. Required Conformance" },
  { number := 192, text := "" },
  { number := 193, text := "Required conformance to this specification holds if and only if every item in this list holds." },
  { number := 194, text := "" },
  { number := 195, text := "1. This specification is number 0016 and the file name is `0016_Hierarchical_Subagents.md` (Clause 1)." },
  { number := 196, text := "2. The layers are `L0`, `L1`, `L2`, and `L3`, with no `L4`. The call name `grok-oss gui` is informative. Specification 0015 does not define those layer names (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 197, text := "3. The naming bans and the report name in Clause 4.2 hold." },
  { number := 198, text := "4. Work that needs tools, as Clause 4.3 describes, runs three layers deep, including implement loops (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 199, text := "5. `L1` keeps the duties in Clause 4.4, does not edit product code or docs, and the fast path is the three acts in that clause and is absent from the task description given to an `L2` (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 200, text := "6. An `L2` coordinates as Clause 4.5 requires and does not do the tool work that clause bans. The two spawn rules named there are nonconforming. Operator clarifications stay on the `L2` (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 201, text := "7. An `L3` does the tool work for Clause 4.3 aside from the fast path, and does not coordinate or spawn (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 202, text := "8. Reports are written under `~/.agents/reports/` on the host, are not written in the repository, and state what changed, how it was verified, what remains, and any question for the operator (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 203, text := "9. Nested exploration and nested implementation wait until the operator Approve (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 204, text := "10. Disjoint write sets run as parallel `L2` coordinators at a sustainable count that this specification does not set to an integer. A shared file runs in sequence. An `L2` stays listed until its own report, and an exit after only spawning or without a report is not finished (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 205, text := "11. A long build has one dedicated `L2`, one job, at nice 19, and that job is not split into several copies at once and is not terminated early. Other work continues (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 206, text := "12. Finished work is the approved plan's owed outcome checked against files on disk, and remaining work goes to that project's residual home (Clause 4.12)." },
  { number := 207, text := "13. A behavior change observes a failing test first (Clause 4.13)." },
  { number := 208, text := "14. A repeated operator instruction is a process defect fixed in a durable place, not by a chat promise (Clause 4.14)." },
  { number := 209, text := "15. A conforming hierarchical subagent program is not claimed (Clause 1)." },
  { number := 210, text := "16. Numbered markdown remains the contract humans read. Lean spec encodings and their proofs stay in separate modules. A mash of those encodings and their proofs does not conform (Clause 1.2)." },
  { number := 211, text := "17. This document does not restate the session bus protocol (Clause 1)." },
  { number := 212, text := "" },
  { number := 213, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming hierarchical subagent program. Meeting these items is a claim about a program that claims this specification. It is not a claim that this markdown file is that program." },
  { number := 214, text := "" },
  { number := 215, text := "The permission in Clause 4.2 item 5 is a MAY. The context budget figures in Clause 4.11 are informative. Those items do not break conformance when unmet." },
